---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout>
  <Fragment slot="head">
    <title>Why this directory exists | Spokane List</title>
    <meta
      name="description"
      content="Spokane List exists so neighbors can share a local contractor in a Facebook group without hunting for a phone, website, or portfolio."
    />
  </Fragment>

  <article class="how-it-works">
    <p class="hero-eyebrow">Why we’re here</p>
    <h1>Share a name that actually helps</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      This directory is for the moment someone in a Spokane Facebook group, Nextdoor
      thread, or neighborhood chat asks “anyone know a good plumber?” You shouldn’t
      need an account—or twenty minutes of digging—to answer.
    </p>

    <section>
      <h2>What usually happens in those groups</h2>
      <p>
        People recommend a name from memory. Then the next comments are the same
        questions: what’s their number, do they have a site, can I see their work?
        Folks scroll old posts, open Google, then hunt for a portfolio that lives
        on a website or Instagram. That’s a lot of work for a neighbor trying to
        be helpful.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>What this is for</h2>
      <p>
        Tap share on a listing. You get a clean note: name, trade, city, phone,
        their website, and a Spokane List link. If their portfolio is on the site
        or Instagram, those links are on the profile too—so the person asking
        doesn’t have to go looking.
      </p>
      <p>
        Filter by trade and city, call from the card, or heart a few names while
        you compare. No signup. Google ratings come along when we have them. You
        still check license and insurance yourself before you hire.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>For the contractor being recommended</h2>
      <p>
        You already get work from groups and word of mouth. This isn’t a second
        profile to manage, and it isn’t a paid listing. Keep your Google Business
        Profile current. When someone shares you, they paste something complete
        instead of a screenshot. The listing stays free either way.
      </p>
    </section>

    <p class="how-actions">
      <a class="button button-primary" href="/">Browse contractors</a>
      <a class="button button-secondary" href="/how-it-works">How sharing works</a>
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
